cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Linked Open Data for the Humanities
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file
  when you refer to it in publications, and/or if you
  re-use, adapt, or expand on the content in your own
  training material.
type: lesson
authors:
  - given-names: Julia
    family-names: Tolksdorf
  - given-names: Robert
    family-names: Zwick
abstract: >-
  This lesson introduces the fundamentals of Linked Open Data using a 
  cultural heritage dataset from the Metropolitan Museum of Art. 
  Learners transform tabular data into RDF, model resources and relationships, 
  explore existing vocabularies and ontologies, and query Linked Data 
  with SPARQL. The lesson focuses on practical, hands-on exercises and 
  assumes no prior experience with Semantic Web technologies.
